{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_10-13-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('logs/695532ca97354c0e88898c9dc4ef75b1/observations.json'))\nev=d['events']; print('total',len(ev))\nfor i,e in enumerate(ev):\n    n=e.get('event'); m=e.get('mode')\n    if n in ('growth_window','growth_write_attempt','growth_recovery','growth_before'):\n        print(i,n,m)\n        for k,v in e.items():\n            if k.startswith('_') or k in ('event','mode','nodes','config_servers','leader','named_server'): continue\n            if isinstance(v,list) and len(v)>4: print('   ',k,'uniq',sorted(set(map(str,v))))\n            else: print('   ',k,json.dumps(v))\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"total 21\n8 growth_before absent_server\n    commit_index 2\n    config_entry_idx 3\n    last_index 2\n    named_server_up false\n    state \"Leader\"\n    term 2\n9 growth_window absent_server\n    commit_samples uniq ['2', '3']\n    config_entry_committed true\n    final_commit 3\n    final_last_index 3\n    final_state \"Candidate\"\n    final_term 2\n    future_error null\n    future_resolved true\n    last_index_samples uniq ['2', '3']\n    leader_state_samples uniq ['Candidate', 'Follower', 'Leader']\n    leader_state_seen_ct 3\n    term_samples uniq ['2']\n    window_ms 1500\n10 growth_write_attempt absent_server\n    commit_now 3\n    write_error \"node is not the leader\"\n11 growth_recovery absent_server\n    config_entry_idx 3\n    elapsed_ms 1531.604635\n    named_server_up true\n    original_commit 3\n    original_last 4\n    original_term 3\n    recovered true\n    states {\"named\": \"Follower\", \"original\": \"Leader\"}\n12 growth_before control_present_server\n    commit_index 2\n    config_entry_idx 3\n    last_index 2\n    named_server_up true\n    state \"Leader\"\n    term 2\n13 growth_window control_present_server\n    commit_samples uniq ['2', '3']\n    config_entry_committed true\n    final_commit 3\n    final_last_index 3\n    final_state \"Leader\"\n    final_term 2\n    future_error null\n    future_resolved true\n    last_index_samples uniq ['2', '3']\n    leader_state_samples uniq ['Leader']\n    leader_state_seen_ct 59\n    term_samples uniq ['2']\n    window_ms 1500\n14 growth_write_attempt control_present_server\n    commit_now 4\n    write_error null\n15 growth_recovery control_present_server\n    config_entry_idx 3\n    elapsed_ms 1517.933637\n    named_server_up true\n    original_commit 4\n    original_last 4\n    original_term 2\n    recovered true\n    states {\"named\": \"Follower\", \"original\": \"Leader\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_10-13-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nR=\\\"695532ca97354c0e88898c9dc4ef75b1\\\"\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpretation of the growth reproduction receipt \\\"+R+\\\" (completed, exit_code 0) for the growth investigation. Parsed events: indices 8, 9, 10 and 11 are the absent-server case (admission, window, bounded write, recovery) and 12, 13, 14 and 15 the control with the named server running beforehand. The predicate evaluated is whether the deposition reproduces under a different schedule; it holds, and the defect claim is unchanged. Both runs of the fixed experiment are cited with the compatibility reasoning needed for two receipts.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"b2266ae85cad4e4db077a5615b2b892c-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"01878d6cc9e24ccb8fd3d9157f560ea3-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"addvoter-doc-staging-promise\\\",\\\"bootstrapcluster-growth-guidance\\\",\\\"appendconfiguration-installs-latest\\\",\\\"commitment-recalculate-quorum\\\",\\\"checkleaderlease-latest-quorum\\\",\\\"quorumsize-latest\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{R:[8,9,10,11,12,13,14,15],\\\"e19ad6d076fa4d878b7bd0f90f067fca\\\":[8,9,10,11,12,13]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"holds\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"666afbbf5c5b4554bbfdd6bc26504c5e-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The AddVoter step with an absent server commits and then leaves the only node a leaderless Candidate that refuses writes until the named server appears.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"b2266ae85cad4e4db077a5615b2b892c-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The lease check and the election path read the latest configuration, so a voter that never answers removes the ability to keep or regain leadership.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Absent-server case in the fresh run (indices 8 to 11): the node starts as Leader at term 2 with commit index 2 and last index 2, calls AddVoter for a server that is not running, and the configuration entry still commits (commit index 2 to 3) while the future completes with no error. The window then shows the sampled states Leader for the first three samples, Follower, and Candidate for the remainder with the term fixed at 2 throughout, so the surviving node lost leadership and cannot be re-elected under the configuration it just committed. The bounded client write is refused with 'node is not the leader' and the commit index stays at 3. Recovery follows the named server being started: the original node becomes Leader again at term 3, its last index reaches 4 and the named node follows. Control in the same run (indices 12 to 15): the node stays Leader in all 59 samples with the same commit progression to 3, the client write succeeds (commit index 4) and the growth completes. The original run of this fixed experiment showed the same sequence with the same values, and the difference between the two runs is scheduling only: node identities are regenerated, and the lease expiry, the election attempts and the transport round trips are independent. Interpretation: the predicate 'the deposition reproduces under a different schedule' holds for the elements the finding rests on - the committed configuration entry with a successful AddVoter future, the loss of leadership within the lease interval, the Candidate state that persists without a term change because pre-vote refuses the campaign, and the refusal of client writes - while the control keeps serving in the same run. This strengthens the earlier single witness into two independent ones without making it a universal claim.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The reproduction uses the same staging and the same library build, so it shows schedule robustness rather than independence from the harness or from in-memory timing.\\\",\n   \\\"The unavailability is repaired by starting the named server, which is the step the documented sequence implies; the finding is about the API reporting success for a step that removes availability, not about an unrepairable state.\\\",\n   \\\"The AddNonvoter scoping result and the in-process repair attempts come from later receipts and are unaffected by this run.\\\",\n   \\\"Both runs end with the named server as a follower; promotion was not part of either.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"One additional run of one fixed experiment, single process, in-memory transport, short timeouts; the unavailability window in this run is bounded by the harness windows (1500 ms) and the recovery poll.\\\",\n   \\\"Only the single-voter growth step was repeated; the configuration shapes covered by the other receipts were not re-run.\\\",\n   \\\"The control and the absent case are separate cluster instances built in the same execution, as in the original run, so the comparison remains between equivalent configurations.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Both receipts are runs of the same fixed experiment: the earlier one is its first run and this one is the repeat requested from the retained inputs, executed from a separate clean copy with identical inputs and its own scheduling. They are not fragments of one history; each is a complete run of the same harness, and they are cited together only to state that the outcome recurred.\\\",\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"单节点集群被 AddVoter 罢免的结果在独立调度下复现\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"对增长实验（固定实验 01878d6cc9e24ccb8fd3d9157f560ea3）从保留输入再做一次干净复现，保留执行 \\\"+R+\\\" 与首次结果一致：对一台尚未运行的服务器调用 AddVoter 后，配置项仍然提交（commit 2→3）且 future 返回 nil；随后采样显示 Leader（前 3 个样本）→ Follower → Candidate，term 全程恒为 2，「预投票」使竞选不会推高任期；客户端写入被拒（node is not the leader，commit 停在 3）；只有当命名服务器在其地址启动后，原节点才在 term 3 重新当选并恢复提交。同一执行中的对照（服务器已先启动）在 59 个样本中始终保持 Leader、写入成功（commit 4）。由于两次运行使用独立干净副本与重新生成的节点标识，租约到期、竞选与传输往返的时序互不相关，说明『一次合法 AddVoter 调用即可罢免唯一节点并使集群写入不可用』不是单一调度的产物。缺陷主张维持不变；这是同一固定实验的第二次完整运行，而非普遍性证明。\\\"\n }]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(upd,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nprint('ok', json.load(open('update.json'))['interpretations'][0]['conclusion'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
